<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyfaidd ap Bleddri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 892</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyfaidd ap Bleddri was king of Dyfed in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> in the later 9th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asser">Asser</a> records that he oppressed the church of St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">Davids</a> and that he submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> in the 880s to protect himself against the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodri-the-great">Rhodri the Great</a> of Gwynedd. He died in 892 and was succeeded by his son Llywarch.</p></div>
